Headings come from a CommonMark parser: lines that only look like headings inside fenced code
(``` or ~~~), indented code, and HTML blocks are skipped, and underlined (setext) headings count.
A ``` line inside a ~~~ fence doesn't close it.
== args
input/guide.md
== file input/guide.md
# Guide

Intro.

Setup
-----

~~~
```
# not a heading
~~~

    # indented code

<!--
# commented out
-->

